        "original_id": "00e97096-d392-5db5-84d3-1d5d07e989c3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Teams: 1928 Philadelphia Athletics, 1928 New York Yankees\n- People: Ty Cobb, Mickey Cochrane, Eddie Collins, Jimmie Foxx, Lefty Grove, Al Simmons, Tris Speaker\n- Roles: baseball player, manager, executive\n- Events: 1928 baseball season, pennant race\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1928 season, the New York Yankees finished with a 101–53 record.\n- In the 1928 season, the New York Yankees won their sixth pennant.\n- In the 1928 season, the New York Yankees finished 2.5 games ahead of the Philadelphia Athletics.\n- In the 1928 season, the Philadelphia Athletics featured seven eventual Hall of Fame players: Ty Cobb, Mickey Cochrane, Eddie Collins, Jimmie Foxx, Lefty Grove, Al Simmons, and Tris Speaker.\n- Eddie Collins was born on May 2, 1887.\n- Eddie Collins, whose full name was Edward Trowbridge Collins Sr., was nicknamed \"Cocky.\"\n- Eddie Collins was an American professional baseball player, manager, and executive.\n- Eddie Collins died on March 25, 1951.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
